## Description

An invoked server-component slot can be hydrated without its serialized argument record. The frames client then treats the function prop as reactive content and invokes it with zero arguments. A normal component callback that reads `props.id` crashes the reactive system.

The SSR HTML contains both the correct button markup and a serialized slot record such as:

```html
<script>
_$HY.r["sc:slot:417cc1de-2-getAboutPage:button#0"] = { id: 10 };
</script>
<!--slot:button#0:start-->
<button>Click me 10</button>
<!--slot:button#0:end-->
```

However, during frame adoption `#resolveSlotRecord("button#0")` can return `undefined`. In `slotsFor`, `ctx.invoked` is therefore false, so the callback itself is returned as reactive content. The range binding later evaluates `source()` with no arguments.

## Minimal reproduction

Enable experimental server components:

```ts
solid({
  serverFunctions: { components: true }
})
```

Create a server function returning a component that invokes a client slot with props:

```tsx
export const getAboutPage = query(async function () {
  "use server";
  const id = 10;
  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1000));

  return (props: { button: (props: { id: number }) => unknown }) => (
    <section>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <props.button id={id} />
    </section>
  );
}, "getAboutPage");
```

Render it dynamically:

```tsx
export default function About() {
  const AboutUs = dynamic(() => getAboutPage());

  return (
    <AboutUs
      button={(props: { id: number }) => (
        <button onClick={() => console.log(props.id)}>
          Click me {props.id}
        </button>
      )}
    />
  );
}
```

Directly load or reload the route containing `About`.

## Actual behavior

Hydration invokes the `button` callback without props:

```text
[REACTIVITY_HALTED] An uncaught error halted the reactive system.
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading "id")
    at About.tsx
    at slotsFor (frames/dist/client.dev.js)
    at #invokeSlot
    at #syncSlots
    at adoptBoundary
```

Making the callback argument optional prevents the crash, but `props?.id` can remain undefined in the click-handler closure. Depending on attempts to defer the callback, Solid can also report the SSR button as an unclaimed server-rendered node.

## Expected behavior

An occurrence encoded as `button#0` was invoked by the server and should hydrate with its serialized argument record (`{ id: 10 }`). The client slot callback should never be called as a zero-argument reactive accessor.

